---
description: >-
  Label syntax with markdownAlwaysOn (#1368, #1400): the source of label-syntax.mmd with the
  setting on, so every label is markdown and the picture differs from the default one. The
  title and both axis titles, one each per chart, are written plain here (quoted markdown
  strings there), so that every label kind shows plain markers read as markdown. The
  plain `**bold** _ital_` rows draw bold and italic and the code-span rows draw inline code, in
  the title, both axis titles, the categories, the legend's plot names and the point labels; a
  quoted markdown string, tags and `\n` draw as in the default mode. A bare backtick outside
  quotes is a lexical error, as in v12, so the bare-backtick form is left out.
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
  xyChart:
    width: 1000
    height: 700
---
xychart
  title "title **bold** _ital_"
  x-axis "x-axis **bold** _ital_" ["cat **bold** _ital_", "`cat **bold** _ital_`", "cat a `code` b", "cat <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O", "cat one\ntwo"]
  y-axis "y-axis **bold** _ital_" 0 --> 10
  bar "plot **bold** _ital_" [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
  bar "`plot **bold** _ital_`" [3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
  bar "plot a `code` b" [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
  bar "plot <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O" [2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
  line "plot one\ntwo" [8 "point **bold** _ital_", 7 "`point **bold** _ital_`", 8 "point a `code` b", 7 "point <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O", 8 "point one\ntwo"]
